# External reference corpora stay out of the repo: corpora/creditcard.arff is ~150 MB and the
# ULB corpus it is built from is DbCL-1.0, so committing it would redistribute third-party
# data. Only the scores it produces are tracked -- publish/README.md caveat 5 and
# reports/pillar1_external_corpus_scorecard.md cite those. Rebuild it from Kaggle
# mlg-ulb/creditcardfraud (convert creditcard.csv to ARFF keeping Time/Amount/Class) and the
# published scorecard reproduces exactly: ULB 0.3745 / 0.1716 / 0.1727%.
corpora/
# Generated benchmark output stays out of the repo. The curated markdown findings under
# reports/ are a different thing: spec/active_slice.yaml and README.md cite them, and an
# ignored report is a dead link for anyone who clones -- so track the .md files only.
reports/*
!reports/*.md
.licenses/

# Ad-hoc scratch scripts and presentation binaries
scratch/
scratch_*.py
*.pptx

# Frontend dependencies
node_modules/
gui/frontend/node_modules/

# Archives
*.zip

# Local staged dataset outputs: track cards and checksum manifests, ignore generated data
staging_*/*.csv
staging_*/*.csv.gz

